/-
# P2 (line p3mc, gen 24): U22, irq's `VSafe9` discharged also at the irq starts whose earliest thread is homed and
# wakes nobody

## The irq starts discharged
`IrqHnAt`: an irq start (`.inl (.irq j)`) where, in `ρ`, the earliest thread `tm` of core `c`'s timer tree (the word
`irqTmW K.ksb c`) is a thread whose `AFFINITY` is `c`, and whose bound notification wakes nobody in `ρ` (`NoWakeR`:
no bound notification, or one neither idle nor waiting, or idle with no bound thread or one not blocked on receive).
Its certificate is `irq_hn_annV` (P2/IrqHnAnn): every word the run reads is kept by the view, so the run at a state
carrying `ρ` on the read set is the run at the view start (accepted fire case without a wake included).

**`irq_annV_hn`** (glue, as gen 23's `irq_annV_fh`), `U22At := U21At ∨ IrqHnAt`, **`serializable_fl4_localU22`**,
**`serializable_fl4_localU21of22`**.

## Premises of `serializable_fl4_localU22` vs `serializable_fl4_localU21`
* **Removed: `VSafe9` [J] at every irq start whose earliest thread of `c`'s tree is, in `ρ`, homed on `c` and whose
  bound notification wakes nobody.** Nothing added; family and start facts unchanged (`fl4LocW11JC` / `StartV2C` [P]).
* Open: `VSafe9` [J] at the irq starts whose earliest thread is homed and whose bound notification would wake a thread
  (idle with `tm` blocked on receive, or waiting), and at the invocation starts; `VSafe` [J] unchanged.

No existing statement changed except the root import list.
-/
